          "reason": "Write log messages as literal strings and close each owned FILE once. Original used the message as fprintf format and closed the same stream twice.",
          "verification": "Actual log.c fails -Werror=format-security, then injected FILE ownership test observes a second close. Corrected code preserves literal100% text and closes exactly once. Evidence c/doodle-log-red.log, doodle-close-red.log and doodle-log-green.log."
        },
        {
          "file": "projeto/kbc.c",
